      "commit": {
        "parents": [
          {
            "commit": "9d550d788f61fe1039662272133d9cc897ea34d6",
            "subject": "DRAFT LU-21180 lod: add lod_prep_md_striped_create KUnit tests"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Ronnie Sahlberg",
          "email": "rsahlberg@whamcloud.com",
          "date": "2026-11-15 07:58:57.000000000",
          "tz": 600
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Ronnie Sahlberg",
          "email": "rsahlberg@whamcloud.com",
          "date": "2026-11-15 07:59:48.000000000",
          "tz": 600
        },
        "subject": "LU-21227 lod: fix stripe count overflow in lod_mdt_alloc_specific",
        "message": "LU-21227 lod: fix stripe count overflow in lod_mdt_alloc_specific\n\nlod_prep_md_striped_create() clamps an overstriped request down to\nmdt_count * lod_max_stripes_per_mdt in a local stripe_count variable,\nand sizes stripes[] and idx_array[] using that clamped value.\nlo->ldo_dir_stripe_count is only updated to the final value after\nallocation succeeds.\n\nWhen lo->ldo_dir_stripe_offset is not LMV_OFFSET_DEFAULT, allocation\ngoes through lod_mdt_alloc_specific(), which read its loop bound from\nlo->ldo_dir_stripe_count directly instead of taking it as a parameter,\nunlike lod_mdt_alloc_qos() and lod_mdt_alloc_rr(). Whenever clamping\nactually shrank the request, lod_mdt_alloc_specific() iterated past\nthe end of the smaller stripes[]/idx_array[] arrays using the stale,\nlarger count, overflowing both heap allocations.\n\nAdd a stripe_count parameter to lod_mdt_alloc_specific(), matching\nlod_mdt_alloc_qos()/lod_mdt_alloc_rr(), and have\nlod_prep_md_striped_create() pass its already-clamped local\nstripe_count instead. Update the existing lod_mdt_alloc_test KUnit\ncallers to pass the new parameter.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nAssisted-by: AGENT:claude-sonnet-5\nSigned-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <rsahlberg@whamcloud.com>\nChange-Id: If60b95760e2a1ce27b18c9048bc249a6d73bf319\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
